    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/assistant-professor-molecular-biologyforensic-biology-department-of-sciences/2725D9DA80A84B4FA750641A8A9D45CE/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Molecular Biology/Forensic Biology, Department of Sciences | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor - Molecular Biology/Forensic Biology, Department of Sciences New York, NY JOHN JAY COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor - Molecular Biology/Forensic Biology, Department of Sciences FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT ABOUT THE COLLEGE John Jay College of Criminal Justice is a senior college of the City University of New York (CUNY) and an internationally recognized leader in educating for justice. Led by President Karol V. Mason, John Jay is a federally designated Hispanic-serving institution, ranked third in the nation in Black student success, and a top-ten institution for promoting student social mobility. John Jay is proud to serve a diverse and dynamic student body of 15,000 students, including nearly 50% who are first in their family to attend college, as well as students who are immigrants, from low-income families, or from other historically underrepresented groups in higher education. The College participates in the doctoral programs of the Graduate Center of CUNY and offers bachelor’s and master’s degrees both in traditional criminal justice-related fields of study as well as in a robust portfolio of liberal arts and sciences programs that highlight themes of justice across the arts, sciences, humanities, and social sciences. POSITION OVERVIEW The Department of Sciences at John Jay College of Criminal Justice invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Molecular Biology, with expertise relevant to forensic biology, to begin Fall 2027. We seek an enthusiastic and collaborative scholar-educator who will contribute to our nationally recognized forensic science programs and help prepare the next generation of forensic scientists. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in molecular biology, genetics, forensic biology, and related areas within the Forensic Science Program, while developing an active research agenda that complements the mission of the Department and the College. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, mentoring, and research. We are especially interested in candidates with the potential to engage students in meaningful research experiences and to develop externally funded projects in molecular biology, forensic biology, forensic genetics, or closely related areas. Candidates should have a record of scholarly productivity or demonstrate strong potential for publishing in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Responsibilities include teaching courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentoring students in research, contributing to curriculum development in forensic biology, participating in departmental and college service, and developing a sustainable research program. The candidate should demonstrate a commitment to working collaboratively with faculty, students, and external partners, be enthusiastic and well-prepared to work with students from a wide range of backgrounds, and demonstrate a commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. As demonstrated in John Jay College’s Seven Principles for a Culturally Responsive, Inclusive, and Anti-Racist Curriculum (https://www.jjay.cuny.edu/john-jays-seven-principles), the College seeks a faculty member who thrives in a multicultural, collaborative academic environment and is committed to both access and excellence in higher education. John Jay College offers a unique opportunity to work in a dynamic academic environment dedicated to justice, science, and public service. The Department of Sciences is home to rigorous forensic science programs that combine strong scientific training with real-world applications, preparing students for careers in forensic laboratories, research institutions, graduate and professional programs, and public service. QUALIFICATIONS A Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Forensic Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, Cell Biology, or a closely related field is required. Professional experience in forensic science, forensic biology, DNA analysis, forensic genetics, or related laboratory practice is strongly preferred. Experience teaching or mentoring undergraduate or graduate students, a strong publication record or evidence of scholarly potential, and the ability to develop an externally funded research program are strongly valued. COMPENSATION $59,256 - $114,091. Salary commensurate with education and credentials CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY If you are viewing the job posting on any website other than CUNYFirst, please follow the instructions below: Navigate to www.cuny.edu Select “Employment” Select “Search Job Postings” Create an Account After creating an account, return to the Job Search page and select “Apply Now” Once you have registered or logged in with your username and password, upload the following documents as a single PDF. Only applications submitted through CUNYFirst are eligible for consideration. •    Cover Letter •    Curriculum Vitae •    Statement of scholarly interests •    Statement of teaching philosophy •    Statement of how you would contribute to the College’s goals for access and academic excellence •    Proof of degree Candidates should have three letters of recommendation emailed to the following address: SCIENCE@JJAY.CUNY.EDU with the subject title as “Job ID 32641 Recommendation letter”. CLOSING DATE The review of resumes will begin on October 2, 2026 The posting closes on November 1, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32641 Location: John Jay College Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/assistant-professor-department-of-economics/815A9FD1998A490883C6967F340A793D/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor – Department of Economics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor – Department of Economics New York, NY JOHN JAY COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor – Department of Economics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT ABOUT THE COLLEGE John Jay College of Criminal Justice is a senior college of the City University of New York (CUNY) and an internationally recognized leader in educating for justice. Led by President Karol V. Mason, John Jay is a federally designated Hispanic-serving institution, it is ranked third in the nation in Black student success, and it is a top ten institution for promoting student social mobility. John Jay is proud to serve a diverse and dynamic student body of 15,000 students that includes nearly fifty percent students who are first in their family to attend college as well as students who are immigrants, from low-income families, or from other historically underrepresented groups in higher education. The College participates in the doctoral programs of the Graduate Center of CUNY, and offers bachelor’s and master’s degrees both in traditional criminal justice-related fields of study as well as in a robust portfolio of liberal arts and sciences programs that highlight themes of justice across the arts, sciences, humanities, and social sciences. The College seeks staff and faculty members who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. POSITION OVERVIEW The Economics Department of John Jay College invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in any field at the Assistant Professor level to begin Fall 2027. The department is dedicated to pluralism and diversity; applicants with a background in heterodox economics are strongly encouraged to apply. The successful applicant will teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, develop curricula, serve as course coordinator, and interact effectively with colleagues to support and enhance department culture. The hiring committee is especially interested in applicants who contribute to the goals of the college through their leadership, community service, research, and/or lived experiences. Candidates are expected to bring enthusiasm and demonstrated commitment to teaching and to develop and maintain an active research and publication agenda. Individuals from demographic groups underrepresented in the economics profession are particularly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate should be enthusiastic and well-prepared to work with students from a wide range of backgrounds and demonstrate a commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Consistent with John Jay College’s Seven Principles for a Culturally Responsive, Inclusive, and Anti-Racist Curriculum ( https://www.jjay.cuny.edu/john-jays-seven-principles ), the College seeks faculty who thrive in a multicultural, collaborative academic environment and are committed to both access and excellence in higher education. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. degree in Economics or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, the potential for scholarly productivity, willingness to participate in course and program development, and the ability to work with others for the good of institution. Candidates are expected to bring enthusiasm and a commitment to teaching, service and scholarship. COMPENSATION Salary commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience within the range of $73,294 - $102,460. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY 1)    If viewing the job posting on John Jay College website or in CUNYFirst, please select the \"Apply Now\" button. If viewing the job posting on any other website, please follow the instructions below: -Go to www.cuny.edu/employment -Click \"Search job postings.” -Click the link for “Faculty” and browse to job Opening ID number 32642 -Click on the \"Apply Now\" button and follow the instructions. Once registered or logged in, candidates should submit the following: an application letter to include how they would contribute to the goals of the College, C.V., research statement, job market paper, and a statement of teaching philosophy, including a discussion of how to create an equitable and accessible learning environment for our students. All items to be uploaded must be combined in a single document preferably in PDF format. 2)    In addition, please have three reference letters sent to EconomicsPosition@jjay.cuny.edu. Here candidates can also submit any supplemental materials, not submitted over CUNYFirst. For additional information email the chair of the Economics Department: J.W. Mason, jomason@jjay.cuny.edu CLOSING DATE Review of applications to begin on October 15, 2026. Position closes on November 1, 2026. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32642 Location: John Jay College Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/queens-ny/assistant-professor-department-of-business-and-economics/AE4BD51C28C04197B501B4A07C19DF94/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Department of Business and Economics)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Department of Business and Economics) | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor (Department of Business and Economics) Queens, NY YORK COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor (Department of Business and Economics) FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT York College, founded in 1966, is a center of academic excellence in the heart of Jamaica, Queens. One of the eleven senior colleges in The City University of New York, the College’s mission is to enrich students' lives by fostering an environment where they’ll grow into passionate and engaged learners. York’s academic programs are housed in three schools: The School of Arts & Sciences, The School of Business and Information Systems, and The School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. Over sixty baccalaureate programs from across a variety of disciplines, including accounting, aviation management, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The College’s 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Department of Business and Economics at York College/CUNY invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Information Systems and Business anticipated to begin Fall 2027. York College is located in Queens, one of the five boroughs of New York City and one of the most ethnically diverse counties in the nation. It is a senior college within The City University of New York and is situated on a 50-acre campus in the heart of the Downtown Jamaica section of the borough. The Department of Business and Economics at York College/CUNY invites applications for Assistant Professor Position anticipated to begin Fall 2027 to teach in the Department of Business and Economics. York College is located in Queens, one of the five boroughs of New York City and one of the most ethnically diverse counties in the nation. It is a senior college within The City University of New York and is situated on a 50-acre campus in the heart of the Downtown Jamaica section of the borough. The individual hired for this position will teach basic and advanced courses in at least one of the following fields: Entrepreneurship, International Business, Business Analytics, Human Resource Management, Marketing, and Economics. Teaching assignments will include evenings and weekends. The successful candidate will provide service to the College, including student advisement, participation on department and college committees, and other assignments given by the Department Chair. Teaching faculty perform committee and department assignments, including administrative, supervisory, and other functions. The successful candidate will: Demonstrate effectiveness in teaching methods appropriate for assigned courses. Assist students with course advising and individual mentoring. Participate in curriculum development as part of the normal workload. Work collaboratively to enhance the Business and Economics department programs with an emphasis on maintaining academic relevance and alignment with marketplace needs. Complete administrative tasks assigned as part of the normal workload. Fulfill bargaining unit workload requirements, including equivalent administrative responsibilities. Serve the College through participation in committees, professional organizations, and community engagement activities. Encourage and support student involvement in student organizations, internships, and career development opportunities. Maintain and develop relationships with the business community and relevant professional organizations. QUALIFICATIONS The successful candidate must possess: A PhD or other relevant doctoral degree in Business, Entrepreneurship, Human Resource Management, Economics, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution by the time of appointment (Fall 2027). Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Academic preparation and teaching expertise in at least one of the following areas: Entrepreneurship, International Business, Business Analytics, Marketing, and Economics. Evidence of commitment to student success through effective teaching, advising, mentoring, and support of diverse student populations. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to service activities within an academic institution, professional organizations, or community settings. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: A strong record of teaching effectiveness and innovative instructional practices, including experience with technology-enhanced learning. Evidence of scholarly productivity, applied research, professional recognition, or contributions to their discipline. An active research agenda with potential for continued scholarly contributions. Experience developing or revising curriculum to address emerging trends in business, economics, and workforce needs. Expertise in emerging and interdisciplinary areas such as AI and business, analytics, digital transformation, entrepreneurship and innovation, sustainability, marketing analytics, international business, or related fields. Significant professional experience or industry engagement relevant to their academic specialization. Experience mentoring students from diverse backgrounds and supporting experiential learning opportunities, including internships, applied projects, and community-based initiatives. Established relationships with business organizations, professional associations, industry partners, or community stakeholders. Experience contributing to interdisciplinary initiatives, accreditation activities, program assessment, grant development, or other institutional initiatives. The Department of Business and Economics seeks candidates who are committed to excellence in teaching, meaningful scholarship, inclusive student success, and strengthening the connection between business education, professional practice, and community engagement. COMPENSATION $82,384 - $98,231 - Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: •    Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. •    Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst •    Click Search job listings •    Click on More search options •    Search by Job Opening ID number 32740 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. CLOSING DATE October 11, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32740 Location: York College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/lecturer-doctoral-schedule-mathematics/617BE724C81344AFB32E5AAC46BAC3DD/job/": {
      "title": "Lecturer Doctoral Schedule",
      "description": "Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics New York, NY BARUCH COLLEGE Apply Now Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT \"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyone’s responsibility” Baruch College, located in the historic Gramercy Park/Flatiron district of Manhattan, is one of eleven senior colleges of the City University of New York (CUNY), housing the Zicklin School of Business, the Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, and the Marxe School of Public and International Affairs. We are proud to serve a diverse and engaged student body of over 19,000. Our students represent a wealth of racial, ethnic, economic, religious, linguistic, and national origin backgrounds, and include many recent immigrants as well as individuals who are the first in their families to attend college. Baruch is ranked among the top institutions of higher education in the nation by The Chronicle of Higher Education for promoting student social mobility. Baruch is also listed among the nation’s top public colleges for academic excellence. Baruch seeks staff and faculty members who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. Visit us at https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/. The Department offers undergraduate majors in Mathematics, Financial Mathematics, Computer Science, and Actuarial Science. The position includes significant instructional responsibilities. The successful candidate should be a math pedagogue, with expertise in teaching lower-division mathematics courses, and will be hired specifically to teach and potentially provide leadership for first-year mathematics courses, including Algebra, Precalculus, and Calculus. Additional responsibilities may include student advising; course and curriculum development; preparation of assessments, program reviews, and collaborative learning activities; participate in faculty and professional development initiatives; evaluation and implementation of innovative methodologies, teaching strategies, and instructional delivery methods; development of teaching materials to enhance student learning and support course objectives; assessment of student learning outcomes; and active participation in departmental, college, and university service activities. QUALIFICATIONS The applicant must have a Ph.D. in mathematics or equivalent, college level teaching experience; demonstrated involvement in curriculum development and experience developing innovative learning materials; demonstrated innovation in the classroom, and implementation of creative and engaging teaching strategies, such as the “flipped classroom.” COMPENSATION $93,080- $104,567; commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. All applications must be submitted online both at Mathjobs.org and at CUNYFirst. The completed application at CUNYFirst will include candidate’s curriculum vitae, answers to screening and self­-identification questions, and an agreement to terms and conditions. A complete application at MathJobs will include an AMS cover sheet, curriculum vitae, at least three letters of reference, which should address the candidate's teaching, a short statement describing teaching philosophy and future scholarship plans. In addition, applicants should submit a narrative statement describing their commitment to working effectively with faculty, staff, and students in a multicultural/multiethnic urban campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered. If you have any questions, please contact HR at 646-660-6590. Application Materials Required at Mathjobs.org: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: AMS Cover sheet Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Multicultural Statement Three or More Reference Letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers at this site) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: http://www.baruch.cuny.edu/math/ Prof. Warren Gordon Baruch College, One Bernard Baruch Way, Box B6-230 New York, NY 10010 CLOSING DATE December 15, 2026 with review of resumes to begin immediately. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32741 Location: Baruch College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/queens-ny/assistant-professor-of-information-systems-and-emerging-technologies-department-of-business-and-economics/44932446102C48D9BE86E4699FC86880/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Emerging Technologies (Department of Business and Economics)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Emerging Technologies (Department of Business and Economics) | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Emerging Technologies (Department of Business and Economics) Queens, NY YORK COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Emerging Technologies (Department of Business and Economics) FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT York College, founded in 1966, is a center of academic excellence in the heart of Jamaica, Queens. One of the eleven senior colleges in The City University of New York, the College’s mission is to enrich students' lives by fostering an environment where they’ll grow into passionate and engaged learners. York’s academic programs are housed in three schools: The School of Arts & Sciences, The School of Business and Information Systems, and The School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. Over sixty baccalaureate programs from across a variety of disciplines, including accounting, aviation management, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The College’s 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Department of Business and Economics at York College/CUNY invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Information Systems and Business anticipated to begin Fall 2027. York College is located in Queens, one of the five boroughs of New York City and one of the most ethnically diverse counties in the nation. It is a senior college within The City University of New York and is situated on a 50-acre campus in the heart of the Downtown Jamaica section of the borough. The Department of Business and Economics seeks a dynamic scholar and educator with expertise in Information Systems and the ability to contribute broadly to the Department’s undergraduate business curriculum. The successful candidate will teach courses in Information Systems and related technology-focused business disciplines, as well as contribute to other business and economics offerings based on departmental needs. Teaching assignments may include courses in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Cybersecurity, AI, Business Analytics, Digital Transformation, Enterprise Systems, Business Technology, and other subject areas in the department such as International Business, Management, Operations Management depending on the candidate’s expertise and departmental requirements. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, and weekend courses. The successful candidate will: Demonstrate effectiveness in teaching Information Systems and other assigned courses. Develop and deliver courses that integrate current technologies, industry practices, analytical approaches, and emerging trends in business. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives within the Department. Mentor and advise students pursuing careers in business, information systems, analytics, cybersecurity, AI, and related fields. Support experiential learning opportunities, including internships, applied projects, industry partnerships, and student organizations. Engage in scholarly research and professional activities consistent with the expectations of a tenure-track faculty appointment. Contribute to department, college, and university service activities. Collaborate with colleagues across business disciplines to enhance program quality and relevance. Maintain relationships with business organizations, professional associations, industry partners, and community stakeholders. Perform other responsibilities assigned by the Department Chair. QUALIFICATIONS The successful candidate must possess: A PhD or other relevant doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Business Analytics, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment (Fall 2027). Demonstrated ability to teach effectively in Information Systems and/or related disciplines. Ability to teach undergraduate courses in Information Systems and contribute to additional courses aligned with departmental needs. Evidence of scholarly potential through research, publications, conference presentations, working papers, or other scholarly activities. Commitment to student success through effective teaching, advising, mentoring, and support of diverse student populations. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Preferred Requirements Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Expertise in Information Systems, including areas such as: Business analytics. Artificial intelligence Digital transformation. Database systems. Systems analysis and design. Cybersecurity. Enterprise systems. Cloud computing. Information technology management. Ability to teach courses across multiple business disciplines, including one or more of the following: Entrepreneurship and innovation. International Business. Management. Marketing. Operations Management. Business Strategy. Economics. Quantitative methods for business. A strong research agenda with potential for continued scholarly contributions. Experience incorporating technology, analytics, applied projects, case studies, and experiential learning into instruction. Experience supporting students from diverse backgrounds and preparing them for careers in business and technology. Professional experience or industry engagement relevant to Information Systems or business disciplines. Experience developing or revising curriculum to address changing workforce and industry needs. Evidence of professional recognition through publications, grants, industry partnerships, leadership roles, or service contributions. COMPENSATION $82,384 - $98,231 - Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: •    Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. •    Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst •    Click Search job listings •    Click on More search options •    Search by Job Opening ID number 32739 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. CLOSING DATE October 11, 2026 (Job posting will be removed at 12am) JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32739 Location: York College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/bronx-ny/assistant-professor-of-political-science-specialization-in-american-politics/7CA71701A90D4FDA8369EDA1FF4F393A/job/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics Bronx, NY LEHMAN COLLEGE Apply Now Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelor’s, master’s, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The College’s community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The Department of Political Science at Lehman College, The City University of New York, invites applications for an Assistant Professor in American politics, beginning Fall 2027. We welcome applications from scholars across the field, and are especially interested in candidates whose research and teaching engage one or more of the following areas: public law, including constitutional law, law and courts, law and society, and American constitutional development; immigration law, policy, and politics, including citizenship; criminal justice and civil rights; American political behavior and institutions, including elections, public opinion, parties, and political participation; American political development; and the intersection of technology and politics, including artificial intelligence. A central service responsibility for the position will be pre-law advising. The appointee will serve as the department’s pre-law advisor and will lead the pre-law program, departmental internships, and the minor in Law and Government. Candidates must be able to teach the department’s introductory course on American government and politics. Responsibilities of the academic appointment include maintaining an active program of scholarship and a robust publication record; developing courses and curriculum and teaching introductory and advanced undergraduate courses; and service to the department and full participation in the life of the College and the University. Obtaining grant funding to support research and institutional initiatives is encouraged. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member are also important. The faculty member may have the opportunity to become involved in graduate programs (master’s and PhD level) at the CUNY Graduate Center. The appointment requires regular on-campus presence for teaching, advising, office hours, and departmental and College activities, although some online teaching or remote administrative work may be involved. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Political Science or related field or J.S.D./S.J.D., in hand by start date. Preferred: J.D./Ph.D.; experience with or commitment to pre-law advising and mentoring students toward legal and public careers; a robust record of teaching and research. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. COMPENSATION $98,231 - $112,841 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Applicants should be prepared to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing samples, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g. sample syllabi, summary of teaching evaluations, teaching statement). Letters of recommendation will be requested for candidates advanced to the semi-finalist round. Review of applications will begin in early October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to joseph.mohorcich@lehman.cuny.edu and elhum.haghighat@lehman.cuny.edu. CLOSING DATE Applications to be received until November 2nd, 2026. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32747 Location: Lehman College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/new-york-ny/lecturer-accounting/33A402692C634102827DF08396567999/job/": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Accounting | City University of New York Skip To Main Content Navigation menu ABOUT History Trustees Chancellor Félix V. Matos Rodríguez Administration Employment Career Success Initiatives Centers & Institutes University Resources ACADEMICS Academic Policy Libraries Academic Calendars Academic Programs Leadership Faculty Affairs Current Initiatives Testing ADMISSIONS Apply Now Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Two-Year Degrees Continuing & Professional Education Online Education Transfer Student Hub Contact Us FINANCIAL AID Tuition and College Costs Student Eligibility Scholarships Student Loans Tax Benefits for Higher Education Applying for Financial Aid Federal and State Grants RESEARCH Research Development & Programs Research Facilities News & Events Research Integrity & Compliance Innovation & Entrepreneurship Office of Research COLLEGES NEWS LOGIN Apply to CUNY CUNYfirst Blackboard FACTS DegreeWorks Navigation menu Keyword Location Military Code SEARCH VETERANS Lecturer - Accounting New York, NY BARUCH COLLEGE Apply Now Lecturer - Accounting FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT \"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyone’s responsibility” The Stan Ross Department of Accountancy is seeking applicants for one lecturer position in Accounting starting Fall 2027, subject to final budget approval. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting. Additionally, the successful candidate is expected to mentor students (undergraduate and master’s students) and undertake significant service to the department. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelors degree plus significant professional experience or Masters degree required in accounting or a related field. Demonstrate an ability and commitment to deliver high-quality teaching in accounting, auditing or taxation. Prior professional work experience in these fields and professional certification (e.g., CPA) are a plus. Successful candidates will be required to participate in Baruch’s “Inclusive Pedagogy” workshop and CUNY’s “Innovative Teaching Academy,” and demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching in a diverse and inclusive environment. Applicants must be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. COMPENSATION $92,359- $106,547; salary commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. To ensure consideration, applications must be received via the official CUNY application system. Candidates should provide a CV/resume. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. CLOSING DATE December 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin September 15, 2026 JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32729 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
